// GENERATED by CMake from the STRATA_MODEL_H / STRATA_MODEL_FF options -- do not edit; edit those.
//
// The engine is specialised to ONE model, and this header is where the CPU expert path's specialisation
// now lives: the pooled activation buffers and the canonical pack form are sized from these two numbers.
// The default (2560 / 640) is the qwen4exp model.  A GLM-5.3-Flash build configures 4096 / 2048, because
// a 4096-wide hidden needs a 4352-byte quantized activation for the widest layer and a 2048-wide expert
// needs 2560, where the built-in buffers hold 4096 and 1024.
//
// Consequence worth stating: the canonical Q2_0 expert form (BLOB and the row/scale counts derived from
// H and FF) is a function of this geometry, so a Q2_0 expert pack built for 2560/640 does not belong in
// a build configured for another model.  Native (GGUF-slice) packs carry their own geometry instead.
#pragma once

